==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|fore-|ground}}. Compare {{cog|nl|voorgrond||foreground}}, {{cog|de|Vordergrund||foreground}}, {{cog|da|forgrund||foreground}}, {{cog|sv|förgrund||foreground}}, {{cog|no|forgrunn||foreground}}, {{cog|is|forgrunni||foreground}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈfɔː(ɹ)ˌɡɹaʊnd/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-foreground.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The elements of an image which lie closest to the [[picture plane]].
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Hampden-Woodberry|author=Mark Chalkley|year=2006|passage=Note the presence in the '''foreground''' of the fronds of ailanthus, often called “ghetto palm,” now ubiquitous in Baltimore but apparently already common in the 1930s.}}
# The subject of an image, often depicted at the bottom in a [[two-dimensional]] work.
# {{lb|en|computing|often|attributive}} The [[application]] the user is currently interacting with; the application window that appears in front of all others.

